0..51 Comment "//! A second-order rule can apply a bound variable."
52..55 Comment "//!"
56..134 Comment "//! `t(u)` instantiates the variable `t` with argument `u`. It substitutes one"
135..193 Comment "//! argument for each variable that the port of `t` binds."
194..197 Comment "//!"
198..271 Comment "//! The higher-order recursive path order proves termination. It puts the"
272..344 Comment "//! instantiation below an application that holds the variable and every"
345..367 Comment "//! argument directly."
368..447 Comment "//! Pattern unification finds each critical pair. The second-order reader joins"
448..462 Comment "//! each pair."
463..466 Comment "//!"
467..500 Comment "//! - see: #2328 — `LetOverlap`"
501..571 Comment "//! - cites: [Jouannaud-1999-the_higher_order_recursive_path_ordering]"
572..650 Comment "//! - cites: [Klop-1993-combinatory_reduction_systems_introduction_and_survey]"
651..725 Comment "//! - cites: [Mayr-1998-higher_order_rewrite_systems_and_their_confluence]"
726..729 Comment "//!"
730..897 Comment "//! [Jouannaud-1999-the_higher_order_recursive_path_ordering]: https://doi.org/10.1109/LICS.1999.782635 \"Jouannaud and Rubio, The higher-order recursive path ordering\""
